X86: emit canonical EVEX packed memory output on Clang

Project unmasked W1 packed moves from the canonical decoder and construct
complete Intel text and operand details through a separate memory writer.
Preserve broadcast-first handling and the caller's validated byte extent.
Share the existing vector-register formatter and retain all output options,
callbacks, reserved-field checks and fallback behavior. Keep the original
static broadcast reader on other compilers.

Verify complete records, protected extents, generated-table reproducibility
and compiler-scoped object identity; include Make, Xcode and MSVC builds.
